Package: taos-desktop-session
Version: 0.1.0
Architecture: all
Maintainer: jaylfc <jaylfc25@gmail.com>
Priority: optional
Section: x11
Depends: greetd, gtkgreet, cage, sway, swaybg, foot, xwayland, taos-wallpapers, taos-gpu
Description: taOS graphical login screen and Wayland session
 A greetd login screen (gtkgreet inside a cage kiosk, interim until the native
 taOS greeter exists) on VT 7, and the taOS session it starts: sway with a
 minimal config, the taOS wallpaper, and one autostart entry point for the
 graphical shell. Both the greeter and the session are limited to the display
 GPU chosen by taos-gpu (/dev/dri/taos-display), so a compute-only NVIDIA card
 never drives the screen. Installing the package does not start greetd and
 does not switch the default target; the taOS login config only becomes active
 with 'taos-desktop enable' ('taos-desktop disable' reverses it). Debian's
 greetd package itself enables its stock unit on first install, so stock greetd
 (text login on VT 7) can start at the next boot until 'taos-desktop disable'.
 The text consoles on VT 1 to 6 are never touched.
